  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Rural Afghanistan 2 - Health Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of Empowering Rural Afghanistan 2 is the empowerment of rural communities by working to reduce poverty and improve resiliency in the face of multiple security, political, social, economic, and environmental threats. ERA II builds on the achievements of the ERA I and IRD programs. 

Training of health staff, nurses and midvwives, for basic health care services, with emphasis is on midwives and mother-child services. Planned activities continue to focus on reducing poverty (SDG1) and inequalities (SDG10) by improving access to healthcare/health personel (SDG3) and gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment (SDG5).</narrative>
  </description>
